<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105064" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῑνακρία</span></b> , ἡ, an old
		name of Sicily, older than <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σικανία</span>
		acc. to <i><span class="en">
			Th.
			6.2
		</span></i>; older than <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θρινακία</span> acc. to
			<i><span class="en">
			Str.
			6.2.1
		</span></i>:—Adj.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρῑνάκριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Call.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			18
		</span></i>, etc.; fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρῑνακρίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Opp.
			<u>H.</u>
			3.627
		</span></i>.—Also written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρῑνᾰκίη</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			D.P.
			467
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Eust.
		</span></i> ad loc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρῑναχία</span></b>  (sic Pap.), ἡ, <i>triple,</i> as epith. of the
			Moon-goddess, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Par.</u>
				1.2525
			</span></i>; written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θρινακία</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				2822
			</span></i>.</div>
